# V1b: the single-card V5 byte gate at FULL scope: selftest, every regime (R1 x5 seeds, R2, R3, R3b, RA, the 2,048-token R4 chain, R5 real text on layers 0, 23 and 47), users 1-3, the two negative controls, the stale-input sequence,
# 100 traced replays with the inputs restaged in place, the program-cache deltas, and the timing arms. Four users x 16 rows, K5-A against V5 bit for bit on raw page images. A full-scope PASS prints the sha256 triple (v5_triple) that
# gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED takes (a later commit; nothing here commits it). READ: 'GDN_V5 verdict=PASS scope=full' and the last JSON line. STOP on FAIL or NO-DECISION; a FAIL with 'bytes>0' is a real difference.
# Runs only if V1a passed. Estimate ~90 min (harness timeout 3 h).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-window and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window runs ONLY on today's production image: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's) and the production profile family
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/v5split/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
